            <div class="prose max-w-none" x-show="lang === 'en'" x-cloak>
                <h2>Conclusion First: Creative Pool Determines Cold Launch Success</h2>
<p>We've seen too many teams blaming cold launch failures on bad products, high pricing, or saturated TikTok traffic pools. However, through serving dozens of cross-border teams, Yiyu Digital Media has discovered a pattern: <strong>when new products fail to achieve positive ROI within 14 days, 80% of the problem lies in creatives, not the product itself.</strong></p>
<p>This isn't emotional judgment—it's based on account data observation. A utility app team cold launching in Southeast Asia ran 23 creative sets in the first week, with only 3 achieving CTR above 1.2%, all of which were native content with high-fidelity usage scenarios. The remaining 20 sets were mostly brand promotional videos and product feature animations with CTR concentrated between 0.3%-0.6%, directly causing $3,000 in spend with negative ROI.</p>
<p><strong>The essence of a creative pool is a probability game.</strong> The larger and more diverse your creative pool, the higher the probability of hitting the platform's traffic pool preferences. But most teams make the mistake of aggressively pushing one set of creatives, panicking when data is poor, and wasting the most valuable cold launch window.</p>
<hr />
<h2>Three Core Stages of Cold Launch Creative Pool Building</h2>
<h3>Stage 1: Direction Verification (Days 1-5)</h3>
<p>The goal at this stage isn't ROI—it's <strong>verifying direction</strong>. You need to run 3-5 creative directions simultaneously, with at least 2-3 creatives per direction.</p>
<p>Yiyu Digital Media's recommended creative direction dimensions:<br />
- Real-person usage scenarios (high fidelity)<br />
- Before/After comparisons<br />
- Pain point solution demonstrations<br />
- KOC seeding style<br />
- Factory/warehouse origin scenes</p>
<p><strong>Core metrics to observe daily are CTR and 3-second completion rate.</strong> Creatives with CTR below 0.8% or 3-second completion rate below 40% should be immediately paused, with budget transferred to better-performing directions.</p>
<p>A home goods category team cold launching in the UK locked in the "real-person usage scenario" direction by day 4 using this method, with CTR stable around 1.5%. Single creative daily spend scaled quickly from $50 to $500.</p>
<h3>Stage 2: Creative Scaling (Days 6-10)</h3>
<p>After direction verification, enter the scaling phase. The core task here is <strong>finding variants of high-performing creatives</strong>, not developing entirely new directions.</p>
<p>Variant strategies for high-converting creatives:<br />
- Change scenarios (same usage flow, different home environment)<br />
- Change characters (different skin tones, age groups, accents)<br />
- Adjust opening hooks (different angle in first 3 seconds)<br />
- Adjust duration (compress 15-second creative to 9 seconds for testing)</p>
<p><strong>The biggest mistake during cold launch is starting over.</strong> You've verified the direction—now iterate on it rather than switching tracks when you see good data.</p>
<h3>Stage 3: Creative Pool Solidification (Days 11-14)</h3>
<p>By this stage, you should have 5-8 data-stable creatives forming an initial pool. Operational focus shifts from "testing" to "maintenance":</p>
<ul>
<li>Set creative decay alerts (CTR declining 15%+ for 3 consecutive days)</li>
<li>Maintain 1-2 new creatives weekly into the pool</li>
<li>Reserve 20% budget for continuous new direction testing to avoid pool aging</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h2>Practical Reminders from Yiyu Digital Media</h2>
<p>The most common mistake during cold launch isn't poor creative quality—it's <strong>too narrow testing dimensions</strong>. Many teams prepare only 3-5 similar-looking creatives without directional differences, test everything and find all data poor, then conclude "this product isn't suitable for TikTok."</p>
<p>In reality, a jewelry store team Yiyu Digital Media served preparing 6 directional creatives for cold launch in the Middle East discovered in the first week that "handmade production process display" had CTR 3 times higher than other directions. This direction later spawned 12 variants, with single creative highest daily spend exceeding $2,000, and the new product achieved positive ROI by day 10.</p>
<p><strong>A creative pool isn't built at once—it's selected through data.</strong> Your task is to build a sufficiently large candidate pool, letting data make the choice rather than betting everything on one creative based on intuition.</p>
<p>If you're preparing for TikTok Shop new product cold launch, welcome to communicate with Yiyu Digital Media's consultant team. We can help you structure creative directions, develop testing rhythms, and monitor data performance, making cold launch less about luck.</p>
